          "heading": "Shared Concept",
          "content": "Both sources rely on distinctions about what genuinely explains or grounds what: one separates full grounds from partial grounds and non-grounds, while the other treats truthmaking and alethic-fact grounding as species of grounding that generate structural counterexamples."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Explanatory Adequacy",
          "content": "The necessity-focused source ties full grounding to connecting questions that lack cognitive significance, with Fine-style essential truths explaining why the grounds imply the grounded fact."
        },
